{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q022_colg_crya_remote_homology","answer":"In SCOPe 2.04, ColG domain d1nqda_/d1nqdb_ was b.23.2.1: the collagen-binding-domain family and superfamily within the CUB-like fold b.23. Cry3A residues 500–644, d1dlca1, was b.18.1.3: the delta-endotoxin C-terminal-domain family within the galactose-binding-domain-like fold/superfamily b.18.1. Thus they shared only the all-beta class; placement in different folds made no SCOPe homology assertion. In current SCOPe 2.08 (latest periodic label 2.08-2026-08-16), ColG was moved to family b.18.1.36 under the same b.18.1 superfamily as Cry3A, while Cry3A remains b.18.1.3. They are therefore different families with distinct specialized functions but are now inferred to be remote homologs sharing common ancestry at superfamily level—not members of one family.

The structural basis is their corresponding compact all-beta, jelly-roll/beta-sandwich cores and strand topology despite very weak sequence similarity. SCOPe’s collagen-binding-family annotation cites PMID 17977833 for likely homology among the 1NQD collagen-binding domain (historical SID d1nqdb_), Cry4Ba domain d1w99a3, and the CPE C-terminal domain d2quoa_. Cry4Ba d1w99a3 belongs to the same b.18.1.3 family as the queried Cry3A domain. As additional structure-based corroboration, 1NQD chain A’s 99.16%-identical ASTRAL representative 1nqjA has a FATCAT match to d1w99a3 with P=0.00395 and initial RMSD 2.52 Å despite only 2.5% identity. This representative result is indirect: the requested 1nqdA hit list itself contained no corresponding stored hit, so the representative’s alignment or coordinates must not be attributed directly to 1NQD.

Functionally, both are noncatalytic terminal recognition modules: ColG’s Ca-bound domain targets collagen, whereas Cry3A domain III contributes to receptor/target binding and insect specificity; the related CPE domain is likewise a receptor-binding module. This shared modular recognition role makes descent with target-specific diversification biologically plausible, although function alone would not exclude convergence. Superfamily membership does not justify transferring collagen binding, Ca dependence, toxin activity, receptor specificity, or individual binding residues between the families. Either structure can guide only the conserved beta-sandwich core as a remote-homology template; family-specific loops, surfaces, ligands, and functional sites require direct structural, biochemical, and sequence evidence.","evidence_used":["/api/v1/","/api/v1/openapi.yaml","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1nqd","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1dlc","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1nqd/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.04/pdb/1dlc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1nqd/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dlc/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1nqda_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.04/sids/d1dlca1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dlca1/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1nqda_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49785/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49785/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/267607/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/49796/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=collagen-binding%20domain&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=17977833&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/search?q=delta-Endotoxin%2C%20C-terminal%20domain&limit=50","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqdA/structure-hits?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1dlcA/structure-hits?limit=100","/api/v1/releases/2.08/chains/1nqjA/structure-hits?limit=100"]}]}
